.DS_Store
# An unanchored `references/`, so it matches that directory name at ANY depth.
# It swallowed the plugin's own `references/` the first time one existed — the
# skill format's standard home for level-3 content (spec-0063 §5) — and a
# gitignored file is invisible to every worktree, so the split committed a page
# whose every pointer resolved to nothing. Nothing tracked has ever lived under
# a `references/` other than the plugin's, so the exception is named here rather
# than the rule narrowed to a directory nobody can now identify.
references/
!.claude/skills/**/references/
!.claude/skills/**/references/**
target/
node_modules/
*.log
.claude/worktrees/

# tools/check-publishable.sh + tools/crates-io-publish.sh --only's own
# `cargo package` CARGO_TARGET_DIR — deliberately NOT under target/, which
# Swatinem/rust-cache walks on every save/restore for the calling CI job
# (tools/lib/package-verify.sh: run 34066557967's ENOENT annotations came from
# exactly that walk finding a directory `cargo package` had just re-extracted
# out from under it). Never committed either way.
package-verify/

# Compiler build output consumed by the validation compose profiles / CI
# (regenerated by `delvec build ... -o validation/delve-output`). The glob also
# covers the extra trees a second `DELVE_OUTPUT` pass builds, e.g.
# `validation/delve-output-cast` (spec-0020's cast-ledger PackTest run).
validation/delve-output*/

# One point of the gallery domain, materialised into a campaign directory by
# `tools/gallery-build.py` so that the tree the bot walks can be rebuilt on
# demand instead of existing only inside a temp dir. Copied out of `gallery/`
# on every run — the SOURCE is `gallery/`, and a committed copy of it would be
# a second gallery, which spec-0039 §2 refuses. Its build tree is covered by
# `validation/delve-output*/` above.
validation/gallery-src-*/

# spec-0023 bot-ladder run artifact (`validation/run-out/run-report.json`): the
# stage results, assist-window ledger, die-retry trials and floor findings the
# `validate` profile's bot writes. A per-run artifact, never committed.
validation/run-out/

# spec-0064's ladder builds its own subject and, under a perturbation, its own
# scratch copy of the build context (`validation/reset-out/<project>` and
# `<project>.scratch`). Per-run, replaced every run, never committed — and the
# perturbation is made on the copy so it can never reach the tree.
validation/reset-out/

# spec-0005 server-jar cache (actions/cache in CI; primed locally). Never committed —
# the Mojang jar is fetched by checksum, never redistributed (ADR-0010).
validation/.jar-cache/

# Server-bootstrap overlay (validation/server-bootstrap-cache.sh): the
# pinned Mojang jar plus the Fabric launch jar and its Class-Path, fetched ONCE per
# job and copied into each ladder's world volume. Never committed and never baked
# into a layer — the jar is fetched by checksum, never redistributed (ADR-0010).
validation/server-cache/

# spec-0006 playtest note-flow artifacts (regenerated by playtest-note-flow.sh:
# captured server log + harvested report). `*.log` already covers playtest.log.
validation/playtest-report.json
# spec-0019 rehearsal-flow artifacts (regenerated by rehearsal-flow.sh).
validation/rehearsal-report.json
validation/shot-patch.json
validation/rehearsal-bot.out
campaigns
# Read-only content-repo clone used by the skin toolchain workflow (spec-0009);
# never part of the GPL code repo.
content-repo/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Machine-local override of delvewright.toml (endpoints, model choices). Never
# committed; it must never hold an API key either — configs name the env var that
# does (docs/reference/i18n.md).
# The local override file and ANY suffixed variant of it. The bare name alone is
# not enough: a scratch copy such as `delvewright.local.toml_test` falls outside a
# pattern that matches only the exact name, and reaches a PUBLIC repo. No key can
# leak either way — the file names an ENV VAR (`api_key_env`), never a value,
# which is what makes a mistake here survivable — but the pattern is what catches
# it.
delvewright.local.toml*

# Owner-private working notes — never committed (stays local even when the
# repo goes public).
docs/notes/private/

# Release-shelf build output (tools/build-release-binaries.sh).
dist/

# Reference-image drafts. The engine repo holds no reference images: an APPROVED
# one is copied into the campaign it belongs to and committed there, in the
# content repo (see [refimg] in delvewright.toml).
.refimg/

# Contact sheets + their score files, same rule: candidate renders laid out for
# the owner to curate massing from (`delvec contact-sheet`,
# `tools/refscore.py`), and the palette swatch sheets under `.sheets/palette/`
# (`tools/block-appearance.py --sheet`), which are tiled Mojang texture pixels.
# Generation-time working material — never shipped, never in the content repo, so
# nothing on a sheet can carry licensing into a delve (ADR-0013) or move its
# bytes (ADR-0006). The tool refuses to write a sheet anywhere else in the repo.
.sheets/

# The opt-in local virtualenv holding the similarity-metric backends
# (open_clip_torch, t2v-metrics). Multi-GB with their PyTorch dependency and
# deliberately absent from CI — see [refscore] in delvewright.toml.
.refscore-venv/

# Local half of the constitution — operating practice, never committed
CLAUDE.local.md
gallery/skins/
# The gallery's stand-in reference images, generated beside the skins by
# prefabs/gallery-generator (--design). `gallery/design.json` — the RECORD — is
# committed; the pictures it names are build output like every other gallery byte.
gallery/design/
# The gallery piece is GENERATED by prefabs/gallery-generator, never committed
# (CLAUDE.md). CI writes it here; so does the documented local command.
gallery-prefabs/
# The gallery build the `gallery` job's own documented command writes locally
# (`delvec build gallery -o gallery-out-en`). CI never sees it - each job gets a
# fresh runner - so it only ever appears on a creator's machine, where it is one
# `git add -A` from a committed second copy of the gallery. Not hypothetical:
# .pyc files and 13 generated .nbt files have reached a branch exactly that way.
gallery-out-en/
# The coverage gate's own report, written by the same documented command
# (`--report gallery-coverage.json --index gallery-coverage.md`). CI uploads
# them as artifacts; on a creator machine they are two more untracked files a
# `git add -A` sweeps into a branch.
gallery-coverage.json
gallery-coverage.md
# The two remaining local outputs the `gallery` job's own commands write into
# the repository root: the render gate's frames (`--frames gallery-frames`) and
# the whole-map illustration path's scratch tree (`--work whole-map-render`).
# Every sibling above was listed and these two were not, which is the same one
# `git add -A` away from a committed copy — and CI never commits, so CI can
# never red on it.
gallery-frames/
whole-map-render/
# `tools/check-gallery-stageable.py`'s work directory: one campaign and one
# build tree per point of the gallery domain, plus the staging gate's reports
# and the admission tokens it mints for them. Deliberately NOT inside a build
# tree — a token where a staging path would find one is how the gallery would
# become stageable (spec-0039 §2).
validation/gallery-stageable/
# The same state, outside the gallery job: the cross-OS determinism digests
# (`--out determinism-<os>.txt`) and the mecha cross-check's hello-world build
# (`-o out`), both written into the repository root by a documented CI command a
# creator also runs locally. `/out/` is anchored because `out` is a directory
# name something deeper in the tree may legitimately carry.
determinism-linux.txt
determinism-macos.txt
/out/
